# The Qottuf BD Board, on this computer. Copy this file to runtime/.env (which git ignores) and fill in what you use.
# Then: npm run board, and open http://localhost:4300.

# ---- The writers: the agents that call Claude. Two ways:
#  claude-plan  your Claude plan. Claude Code on this computer, signed in to your own Claude account, runs each call,
#               so there's no API bill. Install: curl -fsSL https://claude.ai/install.sh | bash   Sign in: claude auth login
#               It's for your own work: a colleague signs in to Claude Code on their own computer with their own account.
#  enabled      an Anthropic API key, billed per use: set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY too.
# Leave it out and the board still runs: code agents (checks, reports, renewals) work, the writers stay off.
QOTTUF_MODEL_CALLS=claude-plan
# Where Claude Code is, if the board doesn't find it, and a model for it (an alias such as opus; unset, the plan's default):
# QOTTUF_CLAUDE_BIN=/Users/you/.local/bin/claude
# QOTTUF_CLAUDE_MODEL=opus
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---- The brand rulebook and fact base: the qottuf-brand skill's folder (it holds references/ and assets/).
# The board looks in ~/.claude/skills first; set this if the skill is somewhere else.
# QOTTUF_BRAND_DIR=/Users/you/path/to/qottuf-brand

# ---- The elevator CRM. Sign in from the board's Elevators page; the session stays in memory and the password is
# never stored. Only if you want the board to sign in by itself at start (an account without two-factor sign-in):
# CRM_URL=https://qottuf-crm.vercel.app
# CRM_EMAIL=
# CRM_PASSWORD=

# ---- The website pages the site check reads, and the domain quotes are sent from.
# WEBSITE_PAGES=https://www.qottuf.com/,https://www.qottuf.com/elevators/simple/,https://www.qottuf.com/elevators/technical/
# MAIL_DOMAIN=qottuf.com

# ---- Where the Ledger lives: an embedded Postgres in runtime/.data/board by default, or a Postgres server.
# QOTTUF_BOARD_DATA=.data/board
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@localhost:5432/qottuf

# ---- The port (the board listens on 127.0.0.1 only).
# BOARD_PORT=4300
